end
```

## Security

### Input Validation
```elixir
defmodule AppWeb.ExampleLive do
  @moduledoc """
  LiveView with input validation.
  """

  use AppWeb, :live_view

  def handle_event("validate", params, socket) do
    changeset =
      %Data{}
      |> Data.changeset(params)
      |> Map.put(:action, :validate)

    {:noreply, assign(socket, changeset: changeset)}
  end
end
```

### Authorization
```elixir
defmodule AppWeb.ExampleLive do
  @moduledoc """
  LiveView with authorization checks.
  """

  use AppWeb, :live_view

  def mount(_params, _session, socket) do
    if authorized?(socket.assigns.current_user) do
      {:ok, socket}
    else
      {:ok, redirect(socket, to: "/unauthorized")}
    end
  end
end
```

## Best Practices

### Module Organization
1. Keep LiveViews focused and single-purpose
2. Use components for reusable UI elements
3. Implement proper error boundaries
4. Use proper naming conventions
5. Document complex business logic
6. Monitor performance metrics
7. Implement proper logging

### Documentation Requirements
1. Document module purpose
2. Document state management
3. Document event handling
4. Document PubSub usage
5. Document security measures
6. Document performance considerations
7. Document testing requirements
